         screen for choosing the home app could open (HOME-01, SRS 8.1). -->
    <string name="default_home_instructions">To make MeeGone your home screen, open the system Settings, then Apps, Default apps, Home app, and choose MeeGone.</string>

    <!-- The About group of Settings, its last (SET-05). -->
    <string name="settings_group_about">About</string>
    <!-- Above the installed version, e.g. "0.1.0". -->
    <string name="about_version">Version</string>
    <!-- The privacy notice (PRIV-04): exactly what PRIV-01 to PRIV-03 and PRIV-05 promise, and
         that the layout and settings join the system's backup (ADR 0018). -->
    <string name="about_privacy">Privacy notice</string>
    <string name="about_privacy_notice">MeeGone has no accounts, analytics, advertising or tracking, and collects nothing about you. Its only connection is to Bing\'s image feed, for the daily image, and those requests carry only the region and image size, never anything that identifies you or your device. Your notifications and app-usage history are read on this device, in memory only; the only usage data kept is which apps you removed from Recent, and when. Your layout and settings are included in the system\'s backup. Uninstalling MeeGone or clearing its data removes everything it stored.</string>
    <!-- The non-affiliation statement (LEGAL-05), word for word. -->
    <string name="about_independent">MeeGone Launcher is an independent project and is not affiliated with or endorsed by Nokia or Microsoft.</string>
    <!-- Opens the third-party code MeeGone includes, with their licences (LEGAL-06). -->
    <string name="about_licences">Open-source licences</string>
    <!-- At the top of the licences, before their full texts. -->
    <string name="licences_intro">MeeGone includes the Rust standard library and the crates it is built with, by the Rust Project Developers and others, under the MIT licence or the Apache License 2.0, at your option. Its Unicode tables are © Unicode, Inc., under the Unicode License v3. The full licences follow.</string>
    <!-- Settings → About → Reset launcher, and the question it asks first (SET-06). -->
    <string name="reset_launcher">Reset launcher</string>
    <string name="reset_launcher_title">Reset launcher?</string>
    <string name="reset_launcher_message">Applications goes back to its first order, without folders and with hidden apps shown again, and every setting goes back to its default. The daily image turns off, and the lock screen keeps the picture it has. The access you allowed stays.</string>
    <string name="reset_launcher_confirm">Reset</string>
    <!-- Shown briefly once the launcher has been reset. -->
    <string name="launcher_reset">Launcher reset</string>
    <!-- First-run setup (ONB-01, ADR 0036): at most four screens, which cover the home views
         until it is finished. It never asks about the theme (ONB-05). -->
    <string name="setup_welcome_title">Welcome to MeeGone</string>
    <string name="setup_welcome_body">Your notifications, your apps and the apps you used recently, side by side. Swipe between them. Setting up takes less than a minute.</string>
    <!-- Moves on to the next screen of setup. -->
    <string name="setup_continue">Continue</string>
    <!-- Declines one thing setup asks for; it can be allowed later in Settings (ONB-02). -->
    <string name="setup_not_now">Not now</string>
    <!-- Setup's second screen: make MeeGone the default home app, with the system's dialog
         (HOME-01). -->
    <string name="setup_default_home_title">Make MeeGone your home screen</string>
    <string name="setup_default_home_body">Then the Home button always brings you back here. Android asks you to confirm.</string>
    <!-- Setup's third screen: the daily lock-screen image, with today's image when online
         (WALL-02). The switch is Settings' own label, "Daily lock-screen image". -->
    <string name="setup_image_body">Each day, MeeGone can put Bing\'s image of the day on your lock screen. Your home screen stays as it is.</string>
    <!-- Setup's last screen: the optional access for Events and Recent (ONB-02). -->
    <string name="setup_access_title">Notifications and recent apps</string>
    <string name="setup_access_body">Both are optional, and you can change them later in Settings.</string>
    <!-- The one plain sentence before each access request: what is read and why (ONB-02). -->
    <string name="setup_notifications_why">MeeGone reads your notifications only to list them in Events, and they never leave this phone.</string>
    <string name="setup_usage_why">MeeGone reads which apps you used recently only to show them in Recent, and that never leaves this phone.</string>
    <!-- Below an access request answered with Not now. -->
    <string name="setup_put_off">Not now. You can allow it later in Settings.</string>

    <!-- The banner over the home views while MeeGone isn't the default home app, at most once a
         day (ONB-04). Its buttons are "Make default" and this dismiss button. -->
    <string name="home_banner_text">MeeGone isn\'t your home screen yet.</string>
    <string name="home_banner_dismiss">Dismiss</string>
</resources>
